source_changes.change:
read_workspace (coding.py:209-219). Keep the os.scandir walk and the DirEntry reparse refusal on listed=item.stat(follow_symlinks=False). Then:
- metadata = os.lstat(item.path);
- repeat the S_ISLNK / 0x400 refusal on metadata;
- if S_IFMT(metadata) != S_IFMT(listed), raise 'Worker workspace entry changed while being inventoried';
- take S_ISDIR, the S_ISREG check, st_nlink != 1 and st_size from os.lstat.
All existing messages are kept and there is no os.name branch.
Verified this session: DirEntry st_nlink 0 vs os.lstat 1 on the repo venv 3.12.13; current read_workspace raises 'non-regular or hard-linked file' on a plain file. No other production DirEntry.stat use exists in src (grep). The optional fd/fstat read-binding hardening is deferred.

Defensive classifier for issue 4; the root cause stays UNKNOWN until NF-1. For provider 'claude' only, and only when _error_fields (failures.py:165-173) has already selected an is_error/error_* result envelope, also read record['result'][:4096].strip().casefold():
- an anchored ^(?:failed to authenticate\.\s*)?api error:\s*(\d{3})\b maps 401 to auth, 408 to timeout, 429 to quota, 500/502/504 to provider, 503/529 to busy, and anything else to None;
- then the existing _NATIVE_DIAGNOSTICS patterns;
- then the anchored ^(?:invalid api key|oauth token has expired|failed to authenticate|please run /login)\b mapping to auth.
Answers with is_error false stay data. This deliberately narrows the 'result text stays data' rule at failures.py:198-199; R2 must sign it off.

source_changes.tests:
pipeline_tests/test_provider_failures.py, parametrized:
- is_error result text 401, 'Invalid API key', 'OAuth token has expired' give ('auth','pool');
- 429 gives ('quota','pool'); 529/503 give ('busy','model'); 500/502/504 give ('provider','model');
- 400 gives 'code'; 'Prompt is too long' gives 'context'.
Negatives: is_error false with 'API Error: 401' gives None; assistant or tool content gives None. Raw text never appears in str(failure).

proposed_fix.change:
Bind the bytes read to the inspected inode, following the pattern at src/cochem_supervisor/releases.py:126-131 and knowledge.py:157-167:

    fd=os.open(item.path, os.O_RDONLY|getattr(os,'O_BINARY',0)|getattr(os,'O_NOFOLLOW',0))
    try:
        opened=os.fstat(fd)
        if (opened.st_dev,opened.st_ino,opened.st_nlink,opened.st_size)!=(metadata.st_dev,metadata.st_ino,1,size) or getattr(opened,'st_file_attributes',0)&0x400:
            raise ValueError('Worker workspace file changed while being read')
        with os.fdopen(fd,'rb',closefd=False) as s: content=s.read(size+1)
    finally: os.close(fd)
    if len(content)!=size: raise ValueError('Worker workspace file changed while being read')

exp1.py shows that os.fstat and os.lstat agree on dev/ino on NTFS.
